---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  API_CREDIT,
  KOROK_NAME,
  MERCHANT_NAME,
  MERCHANT_SHORT,
  PROJECT_LABEL,
  SITE_DISCLAIMER,
  SITE_NAME,
  SITE_TAGLINE,
} from '@/config/site';
import { getSourceMeta } from '@/lib/content';

const meta = getSourceMeta();
---

<BaseLayout title="The Merchant">
  <div class="stack">
    <h1>The Merchant</h1>
    <p>{SITE_TAGLINE}</p>

    <section class="merchant-portraits">
      <figure class="merchant-figure">
        <img
          src="/images/Sorrel.png"
          alt={`${MERCHANT_NAME}, former roadwarden and outfitter`}
          width="160"
          height="160"
        />
        <figcaption>
          <strong>{MERCHANT_NAME}</strong>
          <span class="muted"> — {MERCHANT_SHORT} to the Koroks</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="merchant-figure">
        <img
          src="/images/Pip.png"
          alt={`${KOROK_NAME}, Korok companion`}
          width="160"
          height="160"
        />
        <figcaption>
          <strong>{KOROK_NAME}</strong>
          <span class="muted"> — insists on the detours</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>Meet {MERCHANT_NAME}</h2>
      <p>
        {MERCHANT_NAME} — {MERCHANT_SHORT} to the Koroks — spent years as a
        roadwarden, scouting trails, reading the weather, and getting tired
        travellers safely from one place to the next. They were never much of a
        warrior. Their real skill was preparation: knowing where shelter waited,
        which mushrooms turned up after rain, and how to avoid a fight before it
        started.
      </p>
      <p>
        Somewhere along the way they stopped believing that arriving was the
        whole point. Now they run {SITE_NAME}, a travelling apothecary and
        outfitter for people who want to <em>experience</em> Hyrule, not just
        survive it.
      </p>
      <p class="notice">
        <strong>“You should go. And I want to help make sure you come back.”</strong>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>How the shop came to be</h2>
      <p>
        It started with extra mushrooms. Someone heading into the cold looked
        hopelessly underpacked, so {MERCHANT_SHORT} handed over supplies from
        their own wagon. Then it happened again. And again. Eventually replacing
        everything they gave away got expensive, so they charged a few rupees,
        started tracking what got used, and brought more next time.
      </p>
      <p>
        {MERCHANT_SHORT} still insists this is not a shop. Their Korok friend,
        {KOROK_NAME}, made a sign anyway. The sign stayed.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        {KOROK_NAME}, for the record, maintains that they started the whole
        thing. {KOROK_NAME} cannot be persuaded otherwise.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="stack notice">
      <h2 class="margin-0">Ready for the road?</h2>
      <p class="margin-0">
        The story ends here; the packing does not. Pick a destination, open the
        bench, or browse the shelves.
      </p>
      <div class="home-cta-row">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/regions">
          Where are you headed?
        </a>
        <a class="button" href="/brew">Open the brewing bench</a>
        <a class="button" href="/shop">Shop the shelves</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>About this prototype</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE_NAME} is the in-world storefront for the <strong
          >{PROJECT_LABEL}</strong
        > portfolio project.
      </p>
      <p>{SITE_DISCLAIMER}</p>
      <p>{API_CREDIT}</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Game scope: Breath of the Wild (`{meta.game}`)</li>
        <li>Snapshot retrieved: {meta.retrievedAt}</li>
        <li>Entries: {meta.counts.entries}</li>
        <li>Regions: {meta.counts.regions}</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="stack">
      <h2>Credits</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/gadhagod/Hyrule-Compendium-API">
            Hyrule Compendium API
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Built as a static Astro site with build-time validation and browser-only
          satchel state.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
